    "standard": {
        "explanation": "<h3>Understanding Numbers</h3><p>Numbers are the building blocks of the universe! Let's visualize them.</p><div class=\"number-line-visual\"><div class=\"nl-point\">-3<div class=\"nl-label\">Integer</div></div><div class=\"nl-point\">-2</div><div class=\"nl-point\">-1</div><div class=\"nl-point zero\">0<div class=\"nl-label\">Whole</div></div><div class=\"nl-point\">1<div class=\"nl-label\">Natural</div></div><div class=\"nl-point\">2</div><div class=\"nl-point\">3</div></div><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-tree\"></i> Natural Numbers (N)</h4><p>Counting numbers starting from 1.</p><div class=\"example-box\">Ex: 1, 2, 3, 100... (No zero!)</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-circle\"></i> Whole Numbers (W)</h4><p>Natural numbers plus Zero.</p><div class=\"example-box\">Ex: 0, 1, 2, 3... (The 'Whole' starts with a Hole/Zero)</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-plus-minus\"></i> Integers (Z)</h4><p>Whole numbers plus negative numbers.</p><div class=\"example-box\">Ex: ...-2, -1, 0, 1, 2...</div></div></div><h3>Power Ups (Key Concepts)</h3><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-arrows-alt-h\"></i> Successor & Predecessor</h4><p><strong>Successor</strong>: The number just after (+1).<br><strong>Predecessor</strong>: The number just before (-1).</p><div class=\"example-box\">Successor of 10 is 11.<br>Predecessor of 10 is 9.</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-magnet\"></i> Absolute Value (|x|)</h4><p>The distance from 0. Distance is always positive!</p><div class=\"example-box\">|-5| = 5<br>|5| = 5</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-exchange-alt\"></i> Additive Inverse</h4><p>The number you add to get 0 (The opposite).</p><div class=\"example-box\">Inverse of -5 is +5<br>(-5) + 5 = 0</div></div></div><h3>Number Types (Extended)</h3><div class=\"concept-grid\"><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-balance-scale\"></i> Even & Odd</h4><p><strong>Even</strong>: Divisible by 2 (Ends in 0, 2, 4, 6, 8).<br><strong>Odd</strong>: Not divisible by 2 (Ends in 1, 3, 5, 7, 9).</p><div class=\"example-box\">Even: 2, 4, 100<br>Odd: 1, 3, 99</div></div><div class=\"concept-card\"><h4><i class=\"fas fa-cube\"></i> Prime & Composite</h4><p><strong>Prime</strong>: Only two factors (1 and itself).<br><strong>Composite</strong>: More than two factors.</p><div class=\"example-box\">Prime: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11<br>Composite: 4, 6, 8, 9, 10</div></div></div>",
